{
  "Election": {
    "election_id": "6m3gxq",
    "title": "BV2268 — Two-seat board by Bloc STAR: a fourth candidate wins nothing and changes who does",
    "description": "The same seven voters and the same two seats as the control election, with a fourth candidate on the ballot: Dane. Every score anyone gave Ari, Bea and Cyrus is unchanged; the voters simply also say what they think of Dane. Seat 1 - scores Cyrus 17, Dane 17, Bea 16, Ari 11; Cyrus wins the runoff 4-3, the same winner as before. Seat 2 - Cyrus is removed and Dane's 17 points take a finalist slot, so Ari, who won this seat in the control election, is not even a finalist; Bea beats Dane 4-2 and is seated. So the council goes from Cyrus and Ari to Cyrus and Bea while Dane wins nothing at all - a failure of independence of irrelevant alternatives at the level of the committee. Note what it did NOT need: no Condorcet cycle, and no tie-break. Each seat rebuilds the finalist pair from whoever is left, so an also-ran with a competitive score can crowd out the candidate who would otherwise have won that seat. Full lesson & tabulation: https://masiarek.github.io/star-voting-library/02_STAR_Bloc/03_Criteria/committee_spoiler/index.html",
